#X text 235 140 Trig input;
#X text 123 480 This is the patch used on Sibilla to control the Trigger
input and the “Drone mode” on the module. The switching pin of
the “Trigger Input” jack on Sibilla is directly connected to a
5V line so that “Gate1” input keeps seeing “HIGH” when no cable
is inserted \, forcing the internal envelope to stay open. When a cable
in patched into the Trigger Input \, the switching pin of the jack
is isolated and “Gate1” sees “HIGH” only when a Trigger or
a Gate is sent., f 45;
#X text 52 23 SIBILLA - ©2024 Clatters Machines - All Rights Reserved
, f 56;
#X text 53 41 This is the basic PureData structure to control your
Sibilla. Each Ctrl1 \, 2 \, 3.. corresponds to a specific knob of the
module (see comments). Each knob and the corresponding CV input on
the Sibilla hardware are connected to the same Daisy input via summing
amplifiers so that you can control each “hv_param” with both of
them., f 157;
